{"user": "If I'm playing against someone this good, is there a general rule for the corners that I should just memorize?", "user_ts": "2026-08-12T20:56:26.563289+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 memorize this:\n\n**1. Corners are gold.**  \nIf you can take a corner safely, it\u2019s usually great because it **can never be flipped**.\n\n**2. Don\u2019t play next to an empty corner unless you\u2019ve checked the reply.**  \nDanger squares:  \n- **X-squares** diagonal to corners: **b2, g2, b7, g7** \u2014 often very dangerous.  \n- **C-squares** beside corners: **a2/b1, h2/g1, a7/b8, h7/g8** \u2014 also risky.\n\n**3. Exception:** next-to-corner moves are okay if the opponent **still cannot take the corner**, or if you\u2019ve calculated the endgame and it wins.\n\nShort version:  \n**Take corners. Don\u2019t feed corners. Count the reply, not the immediate flips.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-12T20:56:26.563289+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-12T20:56:31.563289+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
